Z||000004||btoth||10-15-2001||10:05 AM||||I never thought Mustangs were that great, and I always made fun of them myself.  Until I drove a 2001 GT.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I want one! Black, Grey leather, 5-speed... 17" wheels, all that stuff.  For under $20 on A-plan.  Gotta love it.  Definatly what I'm getting after college (unless I'm making a ton of money.. which I don't predict I'll be doing).  I've heard from friends that work at Ford that the Mustangs will be getting smaller again.. anyone hear the same?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fformula88||10-15-2001||10:19 AM||||I have been steering clear of those 'Stang bashing posts for lack of interest ins seeing people bad mouth them here for the millionth time.  However, everyone is entitled to like, or dislike them and that is fine.  <P>I do like them a lot.  Although I think I like the pre-99 styling a little more, the current car is very aggressive and daring from a styling standpoint.  More than I can say about most cars on the road that can be had for any price... much less under $20K.  Even in V6 form they give you a lot of bang for the buck.  190 HP and 0-60 in the low 7's, plus lots of standard stuff.  Try finding a cheaper new car that can beat it and your going to be looking for a while.  RSX Type S, Celica GTS, the WRX, Eclipse GT.. they are all great performers, but are also well over $20K.  For their price, you can be sitting in a Mustang GT which will take this group... the WRX giving it the best competition.  Handling isn't ideal, but its its a lot better than the reputation its solid axle has earned.  The upcoming '04 should be independant at all 4 corners anyway negating the handling differences.<P>Someone will eventually bring up reliability... so do some research before posting.  I have been shopping for a new daily driver and have done some research.  Of course, the RSX and Celica get very high ratings... the WRX is too new to get a good rating and Eclipses tend to have poor ratings.  The 'Stang?  Its rather good.  especially compared to the rest of Fords products and especially compared to its dying GM competition.<P>Ok, I'll climb down off the soap box now.||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||10-15-2001||10:56 AM||||I dont really ever bash any make of car. Everyone has their own likes and dislikes. Theres even people who love there Festiva and Pacer. I am however probably guilty of bashing some of the things people do to their cars, whatever it is. I still live and let live. If some guy has wheels sticking out 18 inches past his fender on a Cavalier, Ill laugh my ass off, but its his car to do whatever. If you paint your car dayglow green, Ill think it looks silly and let it at that. Theres people who dont like my car either but same rules apply, its mine. I dont know what else to say here, so just be tolerant and expect the same.||||reg||1
Z||000007||AusFiero||10-15-2001||11:11 AM||||I haven't been guilty of Mustang bashing as I was looking to buy a 65 Mustang convertible when I bought the Fiero. On the other hand I am very guilty of bashing generation 1 MR2s to rile up the odd MR2 board member that comes across to play. I wont bash the generation 2 ones though seeing I bought one and all.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero2.gif">     <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A><p>[This message has been edited by AusFiero (edited 10-15-2001).]||202.139.20.3||reg||1
