Z||000037||Formula88||10-18-2001||11:59 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>This is generally a good topic, im proud.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>I think though, Mustang owners get pissed off easier when someone talks trash because we get it from everyone, ricers, f-bodys, vettes, fieros, everyone wants to beat mustangs.  its us vs the world, good thing we're equipped to handle it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Do you know why Mustang owners get dissed by everyone?  I'll tell you why.  In general, when the 5.0 came out it was a quick car for it's time.  Not much could hang with it in it's price range.  That lead every "Five-Oh" owner on the planet (or at least every one I've ever met) to act like they have the fastest car on the planet.  They're arrogant and completely clueless to the fact that no matter how fast you are - someone's faster.  THAT's why people give them **** .  Because they deserve it.  Note that this is only for the 5.0 models and later.  Mustang II's were a joke and no one really cares about them.  73 and earlier Mustangs were actually real cars, and their owners aren't nearly as big of jacka$$es.  If you checked, you find that they don't get dissed nearly as much, other than the long time Camaro - Mustang rivalry.<P>I know this is a generalization and a stereotype. It's not meant to reflect on any one person, not even BlackStang95.  It's simply my observation of the Mustang owners I've run across over the last 20 years.  ||||reg||3
